  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a sixteen-song set at Park West in Chicago on October 13, 2008, capturing a mix of acoustic and full-band material [1]. The recording, uploaded by ezralite23, documents the lineup for each track, noting when John was solo, joined by Kaki King on guitar, or played with the full band [1]. The setlist opens with “Have to Explode” and “Heretic Pride” before moving into “Moon Over Goldsboro” and “New Zion” [1]. A highlight is “Wizard Buys a Hat,” a rare track with only four archived performances in the collection [1][2]. The performance includes “The Mess Inside,” which marks the first appearance of that song in thirty-three archived shows after a gap of 1,074 days [1][2]. Listeners can also hear “November Love Song” and “Going to Kansas,” both considered rare with three and twelve archived performances respectively [1][2]. The set continues with “So Desperate” and “Mosquito Repellent,” the latter being the first in the archive with six total performances [1][2]. “Supergenesis” also appears for the first time in the archive, sharing its rarity status with six performances [1][2]. The show concludes with “San Bernardino,” “No Children,” “Sept 15th 1983,” “Michael Myers Resplendent,” and “This Year” [1]. This is the 126th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous recording from May 16, 2008, at the Masonic Temple [2]. The audio file is 74 minutes long and was taped and transferred by ezralite23 [1]. A technical note explains that a loose cable caused a loss of left-channel sound for the first 70 seconds of the first track, which was repaired by splicing in the right-channel audio to balance the mix [1].",
